00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:23.900
A constrained device
is a tiny computer.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.610
It's got its memory,
its processor,

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.830
its analog-to-digital
signal conversion,

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:29.120
all in a single chip.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.040
That's a constrained device.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.020
So because everything's
on that single chip,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.650
it's called constrained because
its memory, its processing,

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:40.022
its storage are all
severely limited.

00:02:40.022 --> 00:02:41.480
This is the class
of computer we're

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.320
talking about when we talk about
30 billion connected devices.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:46.682
