00:22:04.940 --> 00:22:05.440
All right.

00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:10.300
So now I have created a Google
Cloud Pub/Sub subscription

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:13.375
that is associated with the
Google Cloud Pub/Sub topic.

00:22:13.375 --> 00:22:16.490
So now whenever I publish
messages into that topic,

00:22:16.490 --> 00:22:18.430
then they get queued
up in the subscription,

00:22:18.430 --> 00:22:21.560
and I can pull those messages
from the subscription.

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:25.000
So now I'm going to create a
Google Cloud IoT Core registry.

00:22:30.287 --> 00:22:31.870
And I'm not the best
typer and talker.

00:22:35.640 --> 00:22:37.360
And so associated
with this registry

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:39.820
is going to be an event
notification configuration.

00:22:39.820 --> 00:22:43.349
And so what that just
means is, when messages

00:22:43.349 --> 00:22:45.640
are sent-- telemetry messages,
which could be something

00:22:45.640 --> 00:22:48.000
like sensor data from a device.

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:51.220
When those messages
come in, then this

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:53.980
is the topic were those
notifications can go to.

00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:56.770
And so you can also
set this so that you

00:22:56.770 --> 00:22:59.480
can have event notifications
going to other types of things,

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:02.290
and we in the future
may offer other ways

00:23:02.290 --> 00:23:05.110
of connecting with cloud.

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:07.930
So now I've created a registry.

00:23:07.930 --> 00:23:09.730
And after-- now that--

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:13.090
so the registry
will contain devices

00:23:13.090 --> 00:23:18.190
